{"toolCallId":"call_cff792ed9f1340ff969b0e40fe7e0c6c","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"total 128\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 michelkerkmeester  wheel    320 26 Oct 14:57 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 14:50 ..\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   5540 26 Oct 14:56 acceptance-criteria.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel    423 26 Oct 14:50 description.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   5598 26 Oct 14:57 graph-metadata.json\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   3682 26 Oct 14:52 implementation-summary.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  10084 26 Oct 14:52 plan.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 14:50 scratch\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  10926 26 Oct 14:56 spec.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  13028 26 Oct 14:56 tasks.md\n---\n10\n11\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:63:| AC-010 | REQ-010 | Given a warning the script writes to stderr, When it runs with `--quiet`, Then the warning is still written to stderr and stdout stays one line | `rg -c 'exec 2>\\|2>/dev/null' recommend-level.sh` prints `0` and `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null \\| wc -l` prints `0` | Unmet | - |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:91:| REQ-010 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so the flag trims stdout only and never suppresses a warning |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:56:- [ ] T016 Keep the quiet branch off stderr so a warning still reaches stderr while stdout stays one line (REQ-010) (`$S`). Verify: `rg -c 'exec 2>|2>/dev/null' $S` prints `0`.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal